


=Dashboard=

==Description==

The **dashboard** is the main home screen of SaltOS4, where quick access buttons, widgets, charts, and other visual elements can be displayed.

It is not a classic application with forms or records, but a dynamic and fully customizable view designed to provide a quick overview and direct access to frequently used features.

This view centralizes common actions and displays relevant information in a summarized way.

Unlike the previous version, the dashboard now uses **100% of the available screen space** and relies on **GridStack** to manage the layout and organization of its elements.

==Main view==

[../../../../../ujest/snaps/test-screenshots-js-screenshots-dashboard-dashboard-en-us-light-1-snap.png]

The dashboard may include:

- Quick access buttons to applications or frequent actions
- Titles used to group sections
- Widgets that display real-time content (e.g. calendar, emails, charts)
- Charts and information panels

All elements can be easily reorganized using **drag and drop**.

==Dashboard customization==

Dashboard configuration is now integrated directly into the **Dashboard** application itself.

There is no longer a separate configuration application or a gear icon button in the top-right corner.

The layout is managed directly from the main view using **GridStack**, allowing users to:

- Move widgets and blocks using drag and drop
- Resize elements according to the available space
- Freely reorganize the visual layout

Any changes made are **saved automatically** in the user's own configuration, with no additional action required.

This configuration is user-specific and is automatically applied on future accesses.
